  "notes": "{諦|あきら}める means to give up on something, accepting that it cannot be achieved or obtained. It implies resignation rather than simply stopping.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive)\n- Takes を: {夢|ゆめ}を{諦|あきら}める (to give up on a dream)\n\nASPECT (ている):\n{諦|あきら}めている means \"have given up\" — the state of having resigned oneself.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- 〜を{諦|あきら}める: to give up on ~\n- {諦|あきら}めずに: without giving up\n- {諦|あきら}めが{悪|わる}い: reluctant to give up, won't take no for an answer\n- {諦|あきら}めがつく: to come to terms with giving up\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {断念|だんねん}する: to give up, to abandon a plan (formal, often used for decisions)\n- やめる: to stop, to quit (more neutral, less emotional)\n- {手|て}を{引|ひ}く: to withdraw, to pull out (of a project or venture)",
